From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takashi Nakayama <tnak@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:02:02 -0700
Subject: ServiceWorker: Drop ServiceWorkerMainResourceHandle for CSP-sandboxed
 workers

When shared and dedicated worker scripts are received and started, its
PolicyContainerPolicies must be computed and checked to prevent invalid
ServiceWorker from running for the shared/dedicated worker.

This CL ensures the calculation of PolicyContainerPolicies in
DidCreateScriptLoader() and drops ServiceWorkerHandle if the worker is
sandboxed by CSP.

See the bug for details.

Bug: 41478971, 563194341
Change-Id: I8e1df63ea670b10a3bfec73dedd47036ae62dd5e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8461264
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Yoshisato Yanagisawa <yyanagisawa@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Takashi Nakayama <tnak@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712040}

